      "id": "i95dyp5",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "1. What is a Monsoon?"
    },
    {
      "type": "keyFacts",
      "title": "Key Takeaways",
      "items": [
        "Monsoon represents a seasonal reversal of wind patterns caused by differential heating of land and water bodies.",
        "Halley's Classical Theory explains monsoon as a large-scale land and sea breeze mechanism driven by thermal contrasts.",
        "The Modern Dynamic Approach highlights the migration of the ITCZ, upper-air jet streams, and global teleconnections.",
        "The elevated heating of the Tibetan Plateau acts as an atmospheric thermal engine, strengthening monsoon winds over South Asia.",
        "Monsoon variability heavily impacts Indian agriculture, water resource management, and the national economy."
      ],
      "id": "f5ne9hm"
    },
